WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Speaker 1: The Fox News near satire, I mean, it&nbsp;
seems like satire about gas prices declining is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.640
taking on even more comedic proportions. The&nbsp;
new headline on Fox News during a segment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.640
about gas prices, which are down and&nbsp;
I'm going to talk to you about that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:30.720
White House takes a victory lap on a 50 cent&nbsp;
decline in gas prices and FOX reporters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.240
commentators bemoaning and criticizing Joe&nbsp;
Biden. What now? Biden's bragging for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.120
fact that gas prices are down. Well, listen,&nbsp;
if you blame him for gas prices being up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.400
wouldn't you give him some credit for gas&nbsp;
prices being down? And this is a circular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.080
circular firing squad of sorts, as old&nbsp;
as certainly this show has been going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:58.560
If you've got a Democratic president and you're&nbsp;
a Democrat and gas prices go up, you often say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.400
there's no connection between the president and&nbsp;
gas prices. But if it's a Republican, you say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.200
oh, the Republicans to blame for the gas prices&nbsp;
going up. Flip it, gas prices go down and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.720
don't like the guy or gal in the Oval Office.&nbsp;
Well, you don't give them any credit for that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.200
However, if your guy or gal is in the Oval Office&nbsp;
and gas prices go down, you go look at the great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.320
job that they're doing now. I don't do that. I&nbsp;
respect you too much to play that game with you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.760
I've regularly told you presidents have almost&nbsp;
nothing to do with gas prices and we will get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:35.200
to that. But that being said, it cannot be&nbsp;
denied that gas prices are down and they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:42.080
down quite significantly. If you actually take a&nbsp;
look after peaking at $5.02 per gallon nationally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:49.600
they are now down to 449. That is indeed a 53&nbsp;
cent decline to about 11%. I mean, gap gas is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.840
still high. There's no denying that. But&nbsp;
it is a significant, significant decline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:02.000
What can presidents do? What can presidents do to&nbsp;
impact gas prices? There's basically three things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:09.520
One is invade a country that has a bunch of oil&nbsp;
and essentially take it, steal it and use it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.680
then use that to introduce it into the market.&nbsp;
And it presumably, based on the laws of supply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.440
and demand, should reduce gas prices, at least&nbsp;
to some degree. Number two, do a gas tax holiday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:26.560
Gas tax holiday will temporarily lower the&nbsp;
price of gas. And people can stock up on gas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.000
if they want, if there's no limit on how&nbsp;
much you can buy. And number three is tap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.640
into the Strategic Petroleum Reserve. Strategic&nbsp;
Petroleum Reserve can, depending on who you ask,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.920
lower gas prices temporarily between 12 and&nbsp;
$0.18 per gallon. Some people say up to 25.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.560
Slightly different numbers depending on who you&nbsp;
ask. Those are the things a president can do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.960
But if you're Fox News and you've been playing,&nbsp;
the gas prices up is all thanks to Biden to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.360
some degree. Don't you have to give him credit,&nbsp;
credit for prices going down? And just imagine the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:03.440
Fox News editorial meeting. Okay. We can't talk&nbsp;
about rising gas prices anymore. Any other ideas?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:10.480
How about this? Let's slam that. They're coming&nbsp;
down too quickly, that it will hurt gas stations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.240
and that Joe Biden is being braggadocious&nbsp;
about it. That's what they did. That's what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.720
they're doing. When Fox News starts complaining&nbsp;
that the gas prices are falling too quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.360
You start to know something's wrong. And it&nbsp;
wouldn't surprise me to see a headline like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:33.200
Did Joe Biden lower gas prices to distract from&nbsp;
Hunter Biden's laptop? I haven't seen that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.360
That's imaginary. But it wouldn't surprise me what&nbsp;
we did see. And I'm not joking, by the way, about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:46.160
the gas stations thing. We looked at this last&nbsp;
week. Here is Fox News bemoaning lower gas prices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:52.480
because mom and pop gas stations could be hurt.
Speaker 3: I want him to run again and the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.720
probably don't. That is stunning, by the&nbsp;
way, on gas prices. If you had a curious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.840
I was at a lacrosse tournament up in&nbsp;
Wilmington, Delaware, over the weekend in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:07.520
Delaware and northern Maryland. Regular gas&nbsp;
is about anywhere from 455 to 480 a gallon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:11.840
So the price is beginning to creep back down.
Speaker 4: It is. It is. And the point was made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.880
over the weekend, I believe, is The Wall&nbsp;
Street Journal. Gas prices are actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.200
coming back down historically faster&nbsp;
with the price of oil than usual, and.&nbsp;

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.320
Speaker 1: They might be coming down too quickly.
Speaker 4: It goes to show you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:28.640
what an incredible risk reward calculation&nbsp;
has to happen on the part of those small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.680
independently owned, most of them mom and pop&nbsp;
gas stations. It's a struggle for all of them.&nbsp;

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.360
Speaker 1: Now, that's not really true. And&nbsp;
there's a bunch of different things that go into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:44.400
that. Just to quickly refresh your memory, without&nbsp;
going back into it, first, gas stations make very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:51.520
little off of selling gas. That's number one. And&nbsp;
number two, their margin is very similar, whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:57.440
gas prices are high or low. Right. I mean, if&nbsp;
your markup is on average 7 to $0.10 per gallon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.760
if you sell it for five bucks a gallon, you make&nbsp;
7 to $0.10 per gallon. And if you sell it for two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.960
bucks a gallon, you make 7 to $0.10 per gallon.&nbsp;
Sometimes high gas prices are actually bad for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:13.440
gas stations when gas prices are really high.&nbsp;
You will sometimes see gas stations eat a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:19.840
bit of the cost they will accept if everybody's&nbsp;
accepting a seven cent profit. You might see a gas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:26.240
station go. You know what? We make more from the&nbsp;
Slurpees and the ring dings and the honey buns and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.680
the entire thing. So we're going to just eat some&nbsp;
of this price increase to be the cheapest in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:37.520
area. We'll just accept like a 2% profit on gas&nbsp;
or maybe just no profit to get people in buying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:43.840
the higher, higher margin stuff. So not only are&nbsp;
higher gas prices not necessarily good for local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.000
gas stations, sometimes they're actually bad. But&nbsp;
Fox News won't tell you that. They'll just say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.960
Oh, no. What is Joe Biden irresponsible for&nbsp;
so quickly lowering gas prices? But it's also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.360
nothing that he did. But if he did it, then&nbsp;
